<title>USA: Pinnacle Bank Q1 share loss  vs profit.</title>
<headline>Pinnacle Bank Q1 share loss  vs profit.</headline>
<dateline>JASPER, Ala. 1996-10-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>PINNACLE BANK</p>
<p>		    Unaudited Financial Highlights</p>
<p>						   Three Months Ended</p>
<p>						     September 30</p>
<p>						     1996	     1995</p>
<p> Net earnings			  $   (259,000)   $    418,691</p>
<p> Earnings per share			   (0.29)	     0.47</p>
<p> Weighted average shares outstanding   889,824	  889,824</p>
<p>						   Sep 30,	  Jun 30,</p>
<p>						     1996	     1996</p>
<p> Total assets			    191,659,000    186,475,000</p>
<p> Loans receivable			127,400,000    120,644,000</p>
<p> Deposits				  166,384,000    165,234,000</p>
<p> Total stockholders' equity	   14,819,000     15,165,000</p>
<p> Book value per share			  16.65	    17.04</p>
<p> Stockholders' equity to assets ratio     7.7%	     8.1%</p>
<p>NOTE: The bank said that the net loss was principally due to the special assessment of $1.1 million to capitalize the Savings Association Insurance Fund (SAIF) under recently passed legislation.</p>
<p>-- New York Newsdesk 212 859-1610</p>
